# Solarized (light) is BUILT IN to bat, so no theme file or `bat cache --build` step is needed.
# The terminal palette is Solarized Light on every machine (docs/DECISIONS.md, ADR-017).
# If a future bat drops it, bat silently falls back to its default theme. Check with
# `bat --list-themes | grep -i solarized`.
--theme="Solarized (light)"
--style="numbers,changes,header"
--paging=auto
--italic-text=always
